  "reading": {
   "title": "Advice from a friend",
   "text": "Hafsa is tired. She works all day, studies English at night, and sleeps only five hours. On Saturday, her neighbor Linda comes for tea and says, \"You look very tired. Can I give you some advice?\"\n\n\"Please,\" says Hafsa.\n\n\"First, you should sleep more. Seven or eight hours is better. You shouldn't study English after eleven o'clock. Second, you should eat more vegetables and drink more water. You shouldn't put so much sugar in your tea!\" Hafsa laughs. \"Third, you should take a short walk every day. It gives you energy and helps with stress.\"\n\n\"I can walk to the park after work,\" says Hafsa. \"Good idea,\" says Linda. \"You could invite me. I need exercise, too!\" Hafsa smiles. Now she has a plan and a new walking friend.",
